# Pick lists for entry fields (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-19), verbatim intent:

> **When there is a link option ... provide a pick list to choose from as
> well as allowing manual entry. All entry fields ... should provide pick
> lists where they would logically exist.**

## The rule

> **If an entry field's value is drawn from a resolvable set (catalog,
> roster, inventory, plan-of-action items, principals, connection points),
> the operator picks from that set and may still type a value the product
> has never seen. A bare text box for a value that exists in a list is a
> defect. A pick list that refuses a legitimate new value is the opposite
> defect.**

## Required pattern

Use `PickListField` in `pim-offline-server/ui/src/components/PickListField.tsx`
(MUI `Autocomplete` `freeSolo`). Option hooks live in
`pickListSources.ts` so a second adopter of the same set cannot drift.

| Requirement | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| Options | From the real API for that set |
| Typeahead | Client filter; cap the open list when the set is large |
| Manual entry | Default on. Emit `{ kind: 'option', id }` vs `{ kind: 'manual', text }` |
| Fetch failure | Visible error + Retry. The field stays typeable |
| i18n | `components.pickList.*` in `en` and every derived pack |

```tsx
<PickListField
  label={t('…')}
  testId="risk-control-ref"
  value={controlRef}
  onChange={setControlRef}
  options={controlOptions.options}
  loading={controlOptions.loading}
  loadFailed={controlOptions.loadFailed}
  onRetry={controlOptions.retry}
  allowManualEntry
/>
```

## Forbidden

- A free-text field whose value is a catalog id, UUID, finding reference,
  or other resolvable identifier with no pick list
- A select / Autocomplete that cannot accept a typed-new value when the
  product allows records the list does not yet carry
- Silently rendering an empty list when the option fetch failed
- Storing display text in an id column because the control did not say
  which half the operator used
- Lab hostnames, lab accounts, or agent thinking in helper text
- Converting every field in one slice — first adopter is Risk Register
  **link** (control reference, POA&M item). Remaining logical pick lists
  (risk owner, accepted-by principal, and other resolvable entry fields)
  wait for their own slice

## Origin

2026-08-19 — operator: link options need a pick list plus manual entry;
apply that shape wherever an entry field would logically have a list.
